# Schedules and Heartbeats

This Livebook schedules one delayed Signal. It also shows the Heartbeat
declaration for fixed periodic input.

## Install Jido

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)}
])
```

## Define A Scheduled Agent

```elixir
defmodule ScheduleGuide.Agent do
  use Jido.Agent, name: "schedule_guide_agent"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{ticks: Zoi.integer() |> Zoi.default(0)})
    plugin Jido.Plugin.Scheduler
  end

  routes do
    signal_source "/guides/schedule"

    route "schedule.once" do
      action %{delay_ms: delay_ms, observer: observer},
        name: "schedule_guide_once",
        schema: Zoi.object(%{delay_ms: Zoi.integer() |> Zoi.min(0), observer: Zoi.pid()}),
        context: context do
        tick =
          Jido.Signal.new!(
            "schedule.tick",
            %{observer: observer},
            source: "/guides/schedule/timer"
          )

        directive = Jido.Plugin.Scheduler.schedule(delay_ms, tick)
        {:ok, context.agent_state, [directive]}
      end

      define :schedule_once, args: [:delay_ms, :observer]
    end

    route "schedule.tick" do
      action %{observer: observer},
        name: "schedule_guide_tick",
        schema: Zoi.object(%{observer: Zoi.pid()}),
        context: context do
        count = context.agent_state.ticks + 1
        send(observer, {:schedule_guide_tick, count})
        {:ok, %{context.agent_state | ticks: count}}
      end
    end
  end
end
```

## Schedule One Signal

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()

{:ok, agent} =
  Jido.start_agent(
    Jido.default_instance(),
    ScheduleGuide.Agent,
    id: "scheduled-agent"
  )

{:ok, _committed} = ScheduleGuide.Agent.schedule_once(agent, 25, self())

receive do
  {:schedule_guide_tick, count} -> count
after
  5_000 -> raise "Scheduled Signal did not arrive"
end
```

One-shot schedules live in the Plugin runtime. They are not restored after a
complete runtime loss.

## Add A Heartbeat

For fixed periodic input, declare this Plugin in an Agent:

```elixir
defmodule ScheduleGuide.HeartbeatAgent do
  use Jido.Agent, name: "schedule_guide_heartbeat"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{})

    plugin Jido.Plugin.Heartbeat,
      config: [
        interval: 1_000,
        signal_type: "system.heartbeat",
        signal_data: %{}
      ]
  end
end
```

Add one matching route. Every heartbeat enters the normal Agent mailbox and
uses normal admission and Turn rules. A heartbeat is input, not a health proof.

## Stop The Example

```elixir
:ok = Jido.stop_agent(Jido.default_instance(), agent)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

See [Durable Schedule Occurrences](durable-schedule-occurrences.md) for
recurring work that must survive restart.
